Z||000000||Philphine||10-31-2001||05:35 PM||||let me admit strait off i just thought of this on the way to work and haven't looked into it at all, but i know a couple of others are looking for more stereo room too. since i have a coupe with out the aux gauges i'm thinking if the cable is long and/or flexable enough i could get an aux gauge pod and put them there. someone with the guages if it worked could maybe switch to a pillar guages or something.<P>it only just occured to me since i recently got a gt with a pod. that pod looks like the perfect place for something else. it'd be a shorter move with maybe nothing more than making a face plate if the cable will cooperate. give it some thought.<P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||06:18 PM||||There isn't enough depth in the aux gauge pod for the HVAC controls.  I moved mine to the custom ECM cover, but that won't work for you.  There really aren't many other places to mount the HVAC control (believe me...I've spent hours looking!) other than the stock location.  The only other possibility would be a custom made pod in place of the overhead light console.  You'd have to find another (longer) control cable and you'd lose your dome lights, but at least it would be out of the way.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||10-31-2001||06:23 PM||||aw well. it looked doable. i'm still holding the idea for another car where i don't need to move the controls. i have an eq and xover that has a wired remote faceplate. that should fit there.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||10-31-2001||06:25 PM||||A wired remote faceplate would work great there.  Just remember that you'll lose your oil pressure gauge unless you go to a pillar gauge setup.||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||10-31-2001||07:57 PM||||A more viable alternative may be to lose/relocate the center vents.  That way a little more space is opened up. Radio over heater controls, maybe?<BR>Gary||||reg||6
